[Rotproof](https://github.com/secta113/rotproof) keeps the layers and the records in `docs/`. It is pinned in `dev` of
`[dependency-groups]` in `pyproject.toml`, which `uv.lock` locks, and CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) installs the lock
with `uv sync --locked` and runs `rotproof check`.

```sh
uv sync            # makes .venv, the one virtual environment of the project, from uv.lock
uv run rotproof check
```
